                <head>177. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>French Foreign Minister Christian Pineau held a series of wide-ranging talks with
                    United States officials on matters of mutual concern to the United States and
                    France during an official 3-day visit to Washington, June 18–20. During these
                    discussions, Pineau and Dulles discussed the future of European integration
                    efforts. Documentation on these talks is scheduled for publication in a
                    forthcoming <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi> volume.</p>
            </div>
